WEBVTT

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.240
I...

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.090
...really am like a stalker.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:36.950
Masamune Saga

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.070
But...

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.320
...I love him.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.350
It's not like I think that this will bring us closer,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.610
but I can't help it.
I want to know the smallest thing about him.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.130
I just...

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.960
I just love him!

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.620
Having a dream about high-school
right now is a total...

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.620
...nightmare.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.620
Rejected.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.590
I just gave it to you.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.080
Can you please read it properly?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:13.630
I did read it.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.440
What is this proposal?

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.260
You don't feel like doing it, do you?

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.700
Of course I feel like it!

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.650
This is my first project,

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.380
and on top of that, Mutou's work is really popular.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.840
Her work is popular, but there's
no mention of the poll results,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.840
and no plans for any kind of promotion.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.320
I don't even know why anybody should buy this.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.380
Onodera!

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:41.660
Did you think the only job of an
editor is to pick up manuscripts?

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.720
Th-That's not what I...

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.750
I'm aware that you were only editing
big names at your last company.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.010
You probably got used to anything selling.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.310
I didn't!

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.420
You think I can present this at the next meeting?

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.420
Rewrite it.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:58.590
You could have just shown me
the ropes from the beginning!

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.930
Why do I have to teach you anything if you don't ask?

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:05.960
You're the editor-in-chief,

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.310
so shouldn't you be instructing your underlings?

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.650
If you have a question, you should ask me yourself!

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.560
I'm not your mom!

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:19.820
I think you guys ought to deepen your friendship...

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.950
What do you mean? We're all pals!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.560
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.560
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:53.110
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:53.110
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.740
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.740
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.530
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.530
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:08.540
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:08.540
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.370
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.370
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:16.750
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:16.750
If I reach out my hand

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.130
hajimete no kimochi

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.130
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.510
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.510
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.890
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.890
I love you more and more every second

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:34.020
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:34.020
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:42.990
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:42.990
But I want to make it come true

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.450
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.450
Our story continues

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.960
This is bad.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.340
How should I fix this?

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.210
What do you even do for promoting manga?

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.220
A fair?

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.720
I guess I have no choice but to ask Takano...

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.490
No, no, no!

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.610
I don't need his help.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.980
I'll figure this out myself.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.730
What, you're still here?

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.230
Y-You're here, too...

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.810
Well, I'm waiting for a manuscript.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.360
You're still writing the proposal?

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.560
You don't have to worry about me.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.780
Just go home.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.630
Why don't you show it to me?

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.050
It's fine! I can do it by myself!

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:29.870
Come on.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.700
I told you I'm fine!

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:36.830
That was a close one.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.590
You don't have to worry about me.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.050
You can just go home.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.970
The last train will be leaving soon.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.940
Wh-What are you doing?

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.190
I said I'd do it myself.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.470
Liar. You haven't gotten anything done yet.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:52.940
It's fine...

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.730
Come on!

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.380
Don't come close to me.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.610
Do you have the results of Mutou's poll with you?

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.360
Yes.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.250
Did you see how she's always in...

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.400
...the top three ever since she became a regular?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.560
Uh, yes.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.870
What are the sales figures for the works
by the authors in front and behind her?

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.250
Compared to those, how many
do you think you can sell?

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.220
Huh?

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.120
Who's the target audience?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.310
How is it different from the comics
she's produced until now?

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:17.500
Uh...

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.830
How do you want to promote it?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.250
What about flyers? And the point-of-purchase?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.330
One moment, please!

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.690
I'm going to take some notes.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.050
There's more.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.800
What are you going to show on the wrap?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:28.720
And...

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:35.550
Can you do it?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.390
Yes.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.310
I just have to gather the material again,

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.720
and if I put it together...

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.030
What are you doing?!

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.030
What do you mean?

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.350
You were comically serious.
I had to break the tension.

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.450
Can you please stop fooling around?

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.670
I'm trying to do my job seriously!

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.420
Mr. Yokozawa...

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.770
Masamune.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.250
The chief of sales wants to talk to you...

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.180
...about Chiharu Yoshikawa's TV series.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.050
Can you go see him for a sec?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.680
I need to use the restroom.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.750
His editor, Hatori, has already left.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.050
It doesn't matter.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.190
Goddamn it.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:22.560
What are you doing?

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:27.740
Where do I need to go?

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.430
The lounge.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.970
All right.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:42.740
Hey.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.390
H-Hello!

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.330
Is everything all right?

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.080
I thought you were going with Takano.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.090
I was waiting for you.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.850
I'm only going to say this once.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:53.980
All right.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.100
Masamune is mine.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:58.600
Excuse me?

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:04.860
I feel like we might have had a little misunderstanding.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.360
There is nothing going on
between Takano and myself.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.610
Don't give me your flimsy lies.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.170
It's not a lie!

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.030
I'm...

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.120
Yes?

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:18.350
Oh, right.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:20.990
I see. I'll be right there.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.630
Uh, I really have no connection with him...

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.300
Then don't do anything.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.490
Please, wait!

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.260
Yokozawa!

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.260
What the hell was that about?

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.830
There's nothing going on between Takano and me,

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.400
but does this mean that...

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.770
...he and Yokozawa are going out?

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:55.280
I-It's not like it makes any
difference to me if they are or not.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.610
That's right.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.910
It doesn't matter if he's going
out with a man or a woman.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.290
I need to be clear with Yokozawa though.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.280
I don't want him making any
weird assumptions about me.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.530
So what...

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:14.680
...if I liked him a little bit ten years ago?

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.780
Even if Yokozawa somehow knows that,

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.810
it doesn't matter anymore.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.750
It's the last train!

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.410
This sucks.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.530
Takano is probably just...

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.270
...screwing around when he makes passes at me.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.950
For me it's nothing but a nuisance,

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:46.210
and I'm still...really irritated?

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.690
Marukawa Publishing

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:49.710
Takano and Yokozawa's relationship?

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.660
Oh, well, I saw them talking the other day,

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.720
and they seemed very close.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.970
Well, not that it really matters.

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:05.230
I believe they went to the same college.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.170
They did?

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.100
They say it was Yokozawa who got...

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.090
...him into publishing to begin with,

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:17.740
and that he was the one who got
him the transfer into Marukawa.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:24.000
So I guess, yeah, you could say that they're close.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.700
At any rate, they're probably compatible.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.190
Tori!

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.240
Good morning.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:35.470
'Morning.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.120
Good morning...

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:43.700
I sent you an email about
Yoshikawa's project yesterday.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.590
Have you seen it?

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.420
Yes.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.200
I'm going to the sales department right now.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:47.900
Huh?

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.850
I'll see you later then.

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.930
Hatori, wait!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.910
Can you not even say a proper good morning?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.520
I did!

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.540
I didn't hear it.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.620
Well I said it.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.770
If I can't even hear it, what's the point?

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.790
Good morning!

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.670
Good morning.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.790
I'm begging you. Please get to my floor.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.920
I don't want to be alone with him.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:14.800
Onodera.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:20.800
There's some trash...

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.310
I don't want to get involved with
him any further except for work!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.310
Hey!

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.190
I'm tired of getting irritated by...

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.330
...things that are totally irrelevant.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.800
If I stay around him any longer,

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:41.550
I'm going to realize that I'm thinking about him.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:51.900
If it's going to be like this,
I'll just bury myself in work!

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.240
The first thing I'll do is read a butt-load of manga,

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.420
and do some market research!

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.380
Onodera, is that you?

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.150
Saiki?

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.930
It's been ages!

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.930
You never used to read manga,
so when I saw you back there,

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:10.440
I was sure I had mixed you
up with someone else.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.530
Sometimes, I can hardly believe it myself.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.160
But as someone who started at
Onodera Publishing with you,

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:22.480
I'm glad that there's another
manga editor floating around now.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.580
She hasn't changed at all.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.570
Back then,
everyone was always saying that...

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.080
...I only got work through my dad,
and how my connections were unfair.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.080
So good!

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.680
Saiki was the only one...

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.310
...who never cared about stuff like that.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:42.520
Don't you think manga authors lack something...

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.260
...in their DNA for observing deadlines?

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.360
Maybe you should call it a night.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.930
But if you confront them
about it, they explode at you,

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:53.940
and yell, "Hey, I'm doing my best!"

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.860
If you are doing your best, then meet your deadlines!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:03.340
But I love my job so I can't quit.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.270
It's like being in a relationship with a shitty guy.

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:09.480
Should we go soon?

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.120
Shut up, Onodera.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:12.810
What the hell is up with you, anyway?

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.530
A guy's hair shouldn't be all silky like that.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:17.130
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:18.600
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.380
Careful!

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.200
I'm perfectly fine.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.880
Why don't I take you home?

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:24.390
Let's go.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:26.690
Onodera?

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.900
Takano!

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.460
What's he doing here?

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.550
Takano, there are seats over here!

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:40.150
He's with a woman.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:46.870
It's not like I care who he's out with.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:49.160
Takano...

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.940
You mean Takano, the editor-in-chief of Monthly Emerald?!

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.260
Yeah.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.350
Oh no!

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.670
I should've given him my business card!

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:00.650
Damn!

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.380
And I was this close to meeting that famous editor-in-chief!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.180
Takano's famous?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.200
You don't know?

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.800
The Emerald used to be a total rag,

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.430
and he made it into a top magazine in a year.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:14.390
I guess I've heard about that.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.620
Anyway, they say that he doesn't
do anything half-heartedly.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.940
Neither in his work, nor in his private life.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:21.940
His private life?

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.250
They say he's a playboy.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.450
With his looks, it's no surprise.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.630
But these are all just rumors.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.670
Irritation.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.510
Frustration.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.420
I said I don't want to realize it.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.980
He was with a woman.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:44.720
They say he's a playboy.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.220
He was probably meeting her for work.

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:53.010
Then again, they say that
where there's smoke, there's fire.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.980
If there are rumors about it, it's probably true.

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:01.480
Which means that he really was
just screwing around with me.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:05.640
Is that the kind of guy Takano is though?

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.240
I remember him...

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.490
...as more of a loner who didn't
really get involved with other people.

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:15.430
He had his own spot in the library,

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.500
where he'd always go after school and read.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.630
Did you know it's your fault
Masamune's all screwed up now?!

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:26.130
I'm the one who got screwed up.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:28.460
I was really in love with him,

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:30.010
and got destroyed in an instant.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.970
I stopped going to school because of the shock.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.890
In the end, I even transferred to a school abroad.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.720
Thanks to that I've become seriously jaded,

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:43.900
and haven't been able to fall
in love with anyone since.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.070
I guess I shouldn't say "haven't been able."

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.660
It's more like I haven't tried to.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:56.990
Loving someone means entrusting
all of yourself to that person.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:01.420
I can't even imagine doing that right now.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.020
It's too terrifying.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:13.120
G-Good evening.

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:15.130
Didn't expect this sudden rain, huh?

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:21.190
You sure are carefree when you haven't
finished fixing your project proposal.

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:23.960
If you have time to fool around with a girl,

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.440
get your work done already.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:26.880
Excuse me?

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.650
I'm taking care of everything assigned to me.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:33.300
I don't think my private life is of any concern to you.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.780
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.940
What are you doing?!

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.790
I'm saying it because you aren't
taking care of your assignments!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.490
But I am!

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:47.740
You don't have to worry about me!

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:48.870
Please let me pass!

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.420
If you've gotten something done, then I'd like to see it.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:54.100
And who are you to talk?!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:54.680
What?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.180
You were with a girl, too...

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.930
She's an author.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:00.990
Huh?

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:02.810
We had a meeting.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.100
That was Erika Ichinose.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.190
She's one of our authors.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.560
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.490
You're getting worked up about nothing.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.020
This can't be any worse.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.110
Please let me pass!

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:16.000
I want to do some work at home!

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.080
Just do it here.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.160
I want to do my own work my way,

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.460
so can you please stay out of it?

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:21.460
Hey!

00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:25.460
Why don't you just go and play
around with Yokozawa?!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.410
Huh?

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:28.710
What the hell does Yokozawa
have to do with anything?

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:30.380
Well, he's the one with...

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:33.160
...all these strange misconceptions about us.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.340
Now please let me pass.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.720
Yokozawa is just a friend.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.230
You're in my way.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.310
Please move!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:39.810
Onodera!

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.310
You're in love with me, aren't you?

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.090
What are you talking about?

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.360
That's why you have all these misconceptions!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:53.690
You're so full of yourself.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:54.530
Am I?

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.400
Isn't that how it is, or am I wrong?

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.950
Please get out of my way!

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:57.950
Answer me!

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.620
Shut up!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.200
I love you.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.460
Is he stupid?

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.210
How can he even think that I'd
fall in love with the person...

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.520
...I was in love with ten years ago?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.690
It's impossible...

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:21.220
I won't let it happen.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.500
Please stop.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.590
It isn't funny anymore.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.050
What are you doing?

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:35.840
Please stop!

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:38.240
Touch me.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.810
Sto...

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.250
Takano...

00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:43.390
He feels so hot...

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.260
Too hot...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:47.880
I have to stop.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.880
I can't let this go further!

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:59.890
You still haven't answered my question.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.750
Are you or aren't you?

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.150
I will...

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.680
...never fall in love with you!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:12.150
Onodera!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.380
Before we get to that, I want to ask you something.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:28.090
Did you say something weird to Onodera?

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:29.880
Huh, Yokozawa?

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:33.040
I told him to stop sniffing around you.

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.130
What?

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.290
He works for me!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:38.580
What the hell were you thinking?

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:40.920
Is it not your policy to...

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:43.000
...separate your work life and private life?

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:44.770
Yeah, and it's separated.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.190
The hell it is.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.630
You've got to stop screwing around, Masamune.

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:51.060
What are you talking about?

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:54.570
You never get over your past relationships.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.570
Don't you remember what they did to you?

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:02.670
Unless you want to fall apart again,

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:04.260
you should think about what you're doing.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.890
Hey, Masamune?

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:08.540
I need to go to bed. I'm hanging up.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.170
Why?

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.810
Why is my heart still racing?

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.050
Am I a total idiot or what?

00:19:20.310 --> 00:19:23.470
He's just jerking me around.

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:30.480
My first planning meeting.

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:34.100
It's not like I never had one at the old company,

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.020
but I'm still kind of nervous.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:37.230
Onodera!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.960
You forgot your proposal!

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:44.190
Oh, sorry.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:44.990
Are you stupid or something?

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.000
It's only the most important thing for the meeting.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.270
I-I'm sorry.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.200
You don't have to be so nervous.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.450
I already okayed the project,
so there's no way it won't pass.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.740
What the?!

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.830
Is he cheering me up?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.010
Is he making fun of me?

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.350
Good morning.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:06.820
Good morning.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.450
Good morning.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:11.580
These early meetings are such a drag.

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:14.620
Onodera.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:17.560
This is Mr. Isaka, the executive managing director.

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:19.200
It's very nice to meet you!

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.690
My name is Onodera.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.190
The executive managing director?!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:27.100
Mr. Isaka, this is his first meeting, so go easy on him.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.410
Oh, yeah, I saw your proposal already.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:34.290
Pretty good, for a first proposal!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:38.300
That manga's fun, so make sure to push it properly.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.210
Good morning!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.050
Morning!

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.730
Give it your best.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:48.500
He's not one to say something is fun.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:51.930
It means you'll be in the spotlight.

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:54.280
Now what?

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.940
Now I'm really nervous!

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.070
Don't worry.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:04.070
I've got your back if you run into a problem.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:06.950
Good luck.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.870
That's right!

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.710
You're the only son of Onodera Publishing's CEO!

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:16.490
That's right.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:17.710
I see!

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:20.710
I'm the son of this company's CEO.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:23.610
It's not easy when everyone's always
accusing you of riding coat-tails, huh?

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.720
Guys like us need to stick together!

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:31.530
Takano!

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.600
What was all that about you having my back?!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:35.600
Why would I do that?

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.360
Because you're my editor-in-chief!

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.360
One of these days,

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.860
I'm going to pull him off his high-horse.

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.720
I was right, this isn't love!

00:21:45.720 --> 00:21:46.730
This isn't love.

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:49.460
This cannot possibly be love!

